      "mergeID": "6986503a07d7db6a760b8609",
      "mergedPostDetails": "This discontinuity is only present when there are sufficient visible instances with friends to force the \"Online in private instances\" (OiPI) section to below the viewed region of the tab's scroll panel.\n\n1. Open the Social -> Friend Locations\n\n2. Ensure the OiPI section is expanded\n\n3. Slowly scroll down with the controller joystick/mouse wheel \n\n4. Observe the scroll thumb jump down & lengthen slightly when the OiPI section enters the viewed region from the bottom and jump up & shorten slightly when it exits\n\n5. Slowly drag down the scroll thumb with your laser pointer/mouse cursor\n\n6. Observe as in 4, but when the laser pointer/mouse cursor tries to hold the scroll bar at the critical position where the OiPI section is just barely visible, the scroll thumb oscillates rapidly between the two positions & heights mentioned above\n\n7. This rapid movement of the scroll thumb causes the contents of the scroll panel to discontinuously jump between two positions, producing an extremely significant amount of flicker (the attached clip didn't perfectly match the framerate of the game, so there appears to be less flicker than there actually is)\n\nThis affects all builds from when the UI of the main menu was changed.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Jittery scrolling in Social -> Friend Locations tab",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "69864ef60c2608808904b7bf",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
